Oz: the prediction keeps up at any frame rate behind lag. Oz's engine keeps 512 commands (CMD_BACKUP), not
64: at 1000 fps behind 80 ms of round trip and a 20 Hz server's frame, the snapshot's command was older than
all 64, and CG_PredictPlayerState stopped predicting (the view stood still). CG_OldestCmd asks for the
oldest the engine has, down to 64 on Quake3e and ioquake3, which Oz's own servers send this code to. The
prediction starts at the first command past the snapshot's, found looking back from the latest, so the
512 aren't all read each frame.

